      "writtenOn": "2024-12-11T01:35:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e As I understand it, for non-PCM cases that value can also end up being too large. So I think we need to address the minimum buffer size calculation in Module::setAudioPatch as well.\n\nYes, I have overrided `Module::setAudioPatch` and updated the minimum buffer size in it. However, since it\u0027s more experiment like value on different device, it seems doesn\u0027t have a good method to assign a default value in example or make sure vender will update it in their implementation. Maybe adding a new virtual method like `Module::getNominalLatencyMs` do? Do you have better idea?",
      "parentUuid": "c3109ecb_2794c4b6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 185,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 185,
        "endChar": 65
      },
      "revId": "c01d017cad2f2846f67605e697d00b7cccf1f253",
