      "writtenOn": "2024-12-11T18:30:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, we can provide a virtual method `Module::calculateBufferSizeFrames` with a default implementation like this:\n\n```\nndk::ScopedAStatus calculateBufferSizeFrames(AudioFormatDescription format, sampleRate, latencyMs, bufferSizeFrames*) {\n    if (format.type \u003d\u003d AudioFormatType::PCM) {\n        *bufferSizeFrames \u003d calculateBufferSizeFramesForPcm(latencyMs, sampleRate);\n        return ndk::ScopedAStatus::ok;\n    }\n    LOG(ERROR) \u003c\u003c __func__ \u003c\u003c \": format \" \u003c\u003c format \u003c\u003c \" is not supported\";\n    return ndk::ScopedAStatus::fromExceptionCode(EX_UNSUPPORTED_OPERATION);\n}\n```\n\nand then use it both here and in `setAudioPatch`. In the latter, if we can\u0027t calculate the minimum latency, that\u0027s a problem and the error code from `calculateBufferSizeFrames` should be propagated. \n\nHere, in `createStreamContext` if we can\u0027t calculate the minimum latency, that\u0027s also a problem but since `openInput|Output` stream can\u0027t return `EX_UNSUPPORTED_OPERATION`, we should probably just return `EX_ILLEGAL_STATE`.\n\nIn your vendor implementation, I suppose you can provide an implementation of `calculateBufferSizeFrames` which works correctly for all supported formats, and thus the errors outlined above will not be encountered.",
      "parentUuid": "712dff47_63d2b947",
